# Outbound exclusion registries hold identified prospects (name, title, employer, LinkedIn URL)
# for 1,276 people. This remote is PUBLIC, so they are deliberately untracked pending Vadim's
# decision on repo visibility. Regenerate any time from campaign artifacts:
#   python3 scripts/outbound-registry.py backfill --yes
# Revert this block if the repo is made private and the registries should be versioned.
# Per-profile registries only. global-company-registry.json stays tracked: it holds
# company names and coverage, which is not personal data and is worth versioning.
workspace/outbound/exclusions/katerina-registry.json
workspace/outbound/exclusions/nick-registry.json
workspace/outbound/exclusions/olena-registry.json
workspace/outbound/exclusions/katya-registry.json
workspace/outbound/exclusions/vadim-registry.json

# Playwright MCP scratch output (console logs, page snapshots) — not project content
.playwright-mcp/

# content-plan-sync.py keeps the pre-sync CSV so a bad export can be walked back;
# the sheet is the master and content-plan.csv is the tracked copy, so the snapshots are scratch
brand-assets/content-strategy/.content-plan-snapshots/

# Runtime callback tokens for the Telegram approve buttons — session state, and the values are
# bearer-ish. Written by the conductor into the workspace, so it is one `git add -A` from a commit.
marketing_vb/workspace/.callback-tokens.json
workspace/.callback-tokens.json

# The 218 message files Hermes improvised on 2026-09-12 for the uk-erakulis campaign,
# written from a poisoned join (accountants in Guatemala, a hairdresser, "adrew sdasd").
# Kept on disk as the record of what happened — see the directory's own notes — but not
# worth 218 blobs of real names in a public repo. The improvised CSVs next to them stay
# tracked: those are the evidence, the messages are just their output.
workspace/outbound/campaigns/2026-09-01-uk-erakulis-similar/_hermes-improvised-2026-09-12/messages/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Outbound personal data. Added 2026-09-12.
#
# The block above untracks the per-profile registries because "This remote is PUBLIC".
# That reasoning was right and its scope was too narrow: an audit on 2026-09-12 found
# 2,997 distinct LinkedIn profiles — names, titles, employers, profile URLs — already
# published through 63 tracked campaign CSVs, which is more people than the registries
# it was protecting. Every new campaign was adding more.
#
# These patterns stop NEW campaign files from entering. They do not untrack the 63 that
# are already committed, and they do not unpublish anything: the history on a public
# remote still holds every one of those 2,997 people. Only making the repo private
# fixes that, and it is Vadim's call.
workspace/outbound/campaigns/*/people-*.csv
workspace/outbound/campaigns/*/people_*.csv
workspace/outbound/campaigns/*/closelyhq-import*.csv
workspace/outbound/campaigns/*/responses-*.csv
workspace/outbound/campaigns/*/sales-nav-raw/
